Godot skips this whole directory: nothing here is a game resource.

WHY THIS FILE EXISTS -- MEASURED, NOT PRECAUTIONARY. export_presets.cfg
uses export_filter="all_resources", which packs EVERY resource in the
project whether or not a scene references it (see CLAUDE.md, "Piege
payload"). Its exclude_filter covers scripts/dev/* and assets_source/*
but NOT docs/*. So a .png dropped here is imported as a texture and its
derived .ctex ships to every mobile player as dead payload: measured at
414 862 bytes for a single colour sheet, against a ~4.75 MB .pck.

A .gdignore is the narrowest fix available: the engine never scans this
directory, so no .import sidecar and no .ctex are ever produced, and
nothing about the game, the scenes or the export preset changes. Do NOT
"clean this up" -- deleting it silently re-adds every sheet in here to
the download of every player.
